## 4. Sampled textures (type-0x17 pushes of every fragment slot, capture17 + capture18)

Columns: texel base VA (from the record: form 1 `VA = w2 << 4`, form 2 `VA = (w2 & 0x3fffffff) << 2 | 1<<32`), resource and flags from the kernel log (`S8AGX: resource N: ...`; flags 0x80 = caller
memory, 0x82 = IOSurface, 0x0 = stand-in memory; `IOSurface S` from the 'resource N is IOSurface S' line), then the 6 descriptor words. Several records per VA = different views (form 1 attachment record vs
form 2 texture state of the same render target, or the same texture sampled by different passes). The log mixes backboardd and SpringBoard resources; for each VA the LAST covering resource line is shown.

**Facts useful for Agent I** (measured, [H] marks guesses):
* Layer / icon textures live in **caller-memory resources** (flags 0x80): res_105 (0x3c000 B at 0x100c30000, 0x100c40000), res_106 (0x10000), res_107 (0x4000), res_124 (0x3c000). Texel start is at **+0x40** inside
  the resource (`w2 = 0x4030c010` -> 0x100c30040). Their records: w0 = `28b68002 / e0b68002 / a8b68002 / f8b68002` (low 16 bits 0x8002 = format class of the icon textures, high bytes vary:
  b6 = ?, 28/e0/a8/f8 = swizzle or flags [H]), w1 = `00030412 / 00030411 / 00009c15` (size/format field: 0x30412 for the 0x3c000-byte textures, 0x9c15 for 0x10000 and 0x4000-byte ones),
  w3 = `80094000 / 8008c000 / 800ac000` (bit 31 + a value that grows with the texture: 0x94000, 0x8c000, 0xac000 [H: size or stride in 0x100 units]), w5 = `000ffff0` (constant for texture-state form 2).
* A texture-state record has the same shape for the IOSurface textures: res_120 / res_121 (IOSurface 5 = SpringBoard's LA08 surface, 0x4000-byte resource but the real size is in the SweetSurface): `2ca40142 00017207 403a8000 80074000`,
  `fca40142 00000007`, `03050502 00000000 403a8000 80004000` (res_121 / res_122 0x4000-byte caller memory: w1 = 0 and w0 = 03050502: a 4-byte-per-pixel RGBA-like class [H]).
* Render-target textures (res_101 display surface = IOSurface 3: `fc0554c2 00171e2c ...` / `cf8354c2 000171e2 100a5000 00000200`, res_104 / 109..114 stand-in memory) are sampled in form 1 (attachment record)
  and form 2: w0 low 16 bits 0x5982 / 0x464a / 0x54c2 / 0x050a / 0x01ca / 0x54ca, w1 = size field: `0x3641` (694x435), `0x3681` (696x437), `0x0920` (128x74), `0x09a0` (132x78), `0x07e0` (64x64 and 55x55!),
  `0x171e2` (1440x2960), `0x2e1` / `0x802e1` for the capture18 blur chain (sizes not in the dump header; the block dims at +0x690 would give them). 0x7e0 for both 64x64 and 55x55 shows that w1 is NOT the size alone
  (the 55x55 pass renders into a 64x64-aligned allocation [H]).
* 0x5982-class offscreen targets have the extra words `{w3 = 0x8001f200 | 0x800ad200 | 0x80020200, w4 = VA2>>4, w5 = 0x70 / 0x80 / 0x2b0}` (VA2 = end of the pixel plane: a second plane / metadata after the pixels).
* The "form 0" lines at the bottom are pushes whose first 6 dwords are not a texture record (the 0x17 push can point at a block of several records: texture states are 6 dwords, 0x20 apart is not guaranteed; the next
  record starts at +0x18 or +0x20).

```
'@
$body = $ff | Where-Object { $_ -notmatch '^TEX ' -and $_ -notmatch '^# ' }
$progs = @(); $hist = @(); $mode = 0
foreach ($l in $body) { if ($l -match '^## OPCODE') { $mode = 1; continue }; if ($l -match '^## SAMPLED') { break }; if ($mode -eq 0) { if ($l -notmatch '^## FRAGMENT') { $progs += $l } } else { $hist += $l } }
$out = $head + "`n" + ($hist -join "`n") + "`n" + $tail + ($progs -join "`n") + "`n" + $tex + ($tx -join "`n") + "`n```n"
Set-Content (Join-Path $root 'analysis/compositor-frag-forms.md') $out -Encoding UTF8
